  "plain": "A well-known skeptic, Michael Shermer, told the podcast host Jesse Michels about a story that the famous astronomer Carl Sagan once said he thought aliens are real, and that this remark was blacked out of the record. Shermer says he checked with Sagan's widow, Ann Druyan, a friend of his, and she told him it never happened. The story matters because, if true, it would mean a leading scientific voice privately believed in alien visitors."
